```text
MEMORANDUM
TO:

Governing Body, City of Cheyenne
FROM:

Renee Smith, Grants Manager
DATE:

SEPTEMBER 19, 2022
SUBJECT:
RESOLUTION TO ACCEPT FEMA BRIC GRANT – Crow Creek

The City of Cheyenne was awarded a U.S. Department of Homeland Security Federal Emergency
Management Agency FY 2021 Building Resilient Infrastructure Communities grant in the amount
of $180,000.
Grant funds will be used to complete project scoping design work for the Cheyenne Crow Creek
19th Street Crossing Improvement Project.  This project scoping effort/design will evaluate and
identify a feasible, constructible crossing improvement for the 19th Street crossing within the corporate
limits of Cheyenne.
The project’s scope-of-work will include the following tasks: Field surveys and reconnaissance for
collection and evaluation of pertinent data needed for hydraulic modeling of design alternatives including
both bridge and culvert improvements, and digital topographic data development for use in the hydraulic
and geotechnical modeling efforts. The project also includes the development a working hydraulic model
to evaluate and design alternatives.
The total project cost is $240,000, designating $60,000 matching funds from the 1% Drainage Fund.
Grant Narrative: The 19th Street crossing has been recommended for improvements since at least 1988 when
it was discussed in the Crow Creek Drainage Master Study. The crossing lacks adequate capacity and
overtops for moderate flood events, inundating the economically disadvantaged neighborhood to the south
and impacting the traveling public.  In the community’s 1988 Crow Creek Drainage Master Plan, flood
problems were classified as life-safety hazards and/or property damage hazards. The City is interested in
improving the 19th Street crossing and eliminating overtopping to reduce the flood risk for approximately
50 residential and commercial properties.

If you have any questions or need further clarification, please give me a call at 637-6285 or email
at rsmith@cheyennecity.org
```

### Page 2 of 11

```text
RESOLUTION NO. __________

ENTITLED: “A RESOLUTION AUTHORIZING THE ACCEPTANCE OF A FY21
BUILDING RESILIENT INFRASTRUCTURE AND COMMUNITIES
GRANT FOR SCOPING AND DESIGN WORK FOR THE CHEYENNE
CROW CREEK 19th STREET CROSSING IMPROVEMENT PROJECT.”

WHEREAS, the governing body for the City of Cheyenne desires to accept a grant from
the U.S. Department of Homeland Security (DHS) Federal Emergency Management Agency
(FEMA) under the Capability and Capacity Building Activity program; and

WHEREAS, the governing body for the City of Cheyenne recognizes the need to address
critical flood hazards; and

WHEREAS, this Project will result in an application ready construction project for future
funding opportunities; and

WHEREAS, the governing body for the City of Cheyenne accepts a grant amount of
$180,000 toward the cost of the proposed Project; and

WHEREAS, the governing body for the City of Cheyenne agrees to provide $60,000
from the 1% Drainage Fund for the required local match; and

NOW, THEREFORE, BE IT RESOLVED BY THE GOVERNING BODY OF THE
CITY OF CHEYENNE, WYOMING, that a grant contract for $180,000 be accepted from the
U.S. Department of Homeland Security Federal Emergency Management Agency for the
Cheyenne Crow Creek 19th Street Crossing Improvement scoping and design project.

PRESENTED, READ AND ADOPTED this _______ day of ________________, 2022.

__________________________________________

Patrick Collins, Mayor
(SEAL)

ATTEST:
____________________________________
Kristina F. Jones, City Clerk
By Stefanie Boster at 11:22 am, Sep 16, 2022
```

